 35CL c  1976Me12: 0.7-2.1-MeV proton beams were produced from the 1.1-MV       
 35CL2c  Cockroft-Walton and a 3-MV Van de Graaff accelerator. Targets were ZnS 
 35CL3c  (46% {+34}S) and CdS (37% {+34}S) on tantalum backings. |g rays were   
 35CL4c  detected using a 10-cm by 10-cm NaI detector and a 40-cm{+3} Ge(Li)    
 35CL5c  detector. Measured |s(E{-p}), E|g, |g(|q). Deduced level energies for  
 35CL6c  33 bound states and 47 resonances, J, |p, resonance strengths, |g      
 35CL7c  branching ratios, mixing ratios, and lifetimes for 25 bound states     
 35CL8c  using DSAM.                                                            
 35CL d                                                                         
 35CL c  1976Sp08: 1.21,1.95-2.91-MeV protons were produced from the Utrecht    
 35CL2c  University 3-MV Van de Graaff accelerator. Targets were Ag{+2}S (95%   
 35CL3c  {+34}) evaporated onto a tantalum backing. |g rays were detected using 
 35CL4c  a 10 cm by 10 cm diameter NaI scintillator and a 120- or 60-cm{+3}     
 35CL5c  Ge(Li) detector. Measured reaction yields, E|g. Deduced Q value, 84    
 35CL6c  resonance energies, resonance strengths, widths, J, |p, and            
 35CL7c  |g-branching ratios.                                                   
 35CL c  1976Sp09: similar setup as 1976Sp08 with 2.33-2.79-MeV protons.        
 35CL2c  Measured reaction yields, E|g, |g(|q). Deduced levels, J, |p, and      
 35CL3c  |g-branching ratios.                                                   
 35CL d                                                                         
 35CL c  1972Hu10: 0.7-2.1-MeV protons were produced from the 4-MV Van de Graaff
 35CL2c  the Centre d'Etudes Nucleaires de Bordeaux-Gradignan. Targets were     
 35CL3c  100-|mg/cm{+2} Ag{-2}S (90% {+34}S). |g rays were detected using a     
 35CL4c  12.7-cm by 12.7-cm NaI(Tl) detector and a 60-cm{+3} Ge(Li) detector.   
 35CL5c  Measured |s(E{-p}), E|g, I|g. Deduced 59 resonances, 32 bound states,  
 35CL6c  resonance strengths, and |g branching ratios.                          
